Subject: [PATCH] Start fullscreen windows below a pinned panel's inset marker

Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Yakymenko
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Apply after patches 0001 through 0012 on niri v26.04. A mapped layer surface
with the namespace emaki-fullscreen-inset from the trusted shell connection
(patch 0010), anchored to the top edge and not to the bottom, sets a top inset
for fullscreen tiles on its output: its requested height plus its top margin.
The same namespace from any other client is ignored. Fullscreen tiles start
below the inset and receive the remaining output height; their configure, size
clamps, render and input origins follow. The marker reserves no working area,
so normal and maximized windows never resize when it maps or unmaps. Without
the marker, fullscreen stays edge to edge as upstream. The IPC tile position is
reported only for an inset fullscreen scrolling tile, so a shell can recognize
it.

